# rustup provides cargo and rustc: rules builds with RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=stable, whose toolchain
# tools/debian-build installs. The rest are what the binaries and helpers link, and, after
# dbus, what the tests need: a private session bus, pixman for the headless backend,
# libwayland-client for the fixture's clients and the Xwayland the X11 tier spawns, and
# python-dbusmock, the BlueZ caminito-bluetooth's tests run against (255) and the
# NetworkManager caminito-network's and the Network applet's run against.
# libaudit-dev: Ubuntu's pam.pc requires audit's, and libpam0g-dev doesn't bring it.
# libmate-panel-applet-dev has the applet library the Bluetooth applet is built against (259,
# ADR 0035). It's the patched mate-panel's, at its baseline, which no stock version reaches
# (ADR 0029): Ubuntu's .so.1 library is not the one the patched panel loads applets with.
# libsensors-dev is lm_sensors' library, which the Thermal applet reads its temperatures and
# fans through (267). The applet links libsensors5, which ${shlibs:Depends} brings at run time
# (270).
# libnm-dev is NetworkManager's client library, which the Network applet reads it through (ADR
# 0041). The applet links libnm0, which ${shlibs:Depends} brings at run time.
# libxfce4windowing-dev is the library the Dock applet reads the windows through (CMN-219, ADR
# 0013), and libgtk-layer-shell-dev the layer surface its test probe is. libwayland-dev's
# wayland-scanner makes the xdg-activation client the applet asks for a launch's token with
# (CMN-221), from the XML it vendors.
