# ${shlibs:Depends} has what the binaries and helpers link. The rest is what caminito-git's
# depends names at run time, by Ubuntu's names: librsvg's pixbuf loader for SVG theme
# images, Menta from mate-themes, the Xwayland it spawns, glvnd's libEGL and mesa's drivers,
# which it dlopens for GBM, zenity for Marco's two dialogs, mate-screensaver's PAM service and
# lock dialogs for caminito-locker, the notification daemon and polkit agent mate-session
# autostarts, hicolor's directory for the logo, and mate-desktop's org.mate.background, which
# caminito-wallpaperd reads on its first run, and glib-networking, GIO's TLS, which it fetches
# a picture of the day with, and bluez, the daemon caminito-bluetooth and the Bluetooth applet
# talk to (255, 259), and upower, which the Power applet reads the batteries from (262).
# power-profiles-daemon has the power profiles of the applet's popup (264), which has none
# without it. nm-connection-editor is the Network applet's settings window, which it also runs
# for an Enterprise network and a hidden one (ADR 0041): without it, those buttons only log
# that it can't run. gvfs serves the Dock applet's Trash, trash:/// (CMN-220), as it does
# Caja.
# The patched packages and marco join these in ticket 205, at versions no stock one has.
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 librsvg2-common,
 mate-themes,
 xwayland,
 libegl1,
 libegl-mesa0,
 libgl1-mesa-dri,
 glib-networking,
 zenity,
 mate-screensaver,
 mate-notification-daemon,
 mate-polkit,
 hicolor-icon-theme,
 mate-desktop-common,
 bluez,
 upower,
 gvfs,
# The GTK module's caminito version, which installs the file the session adds the module by
# (192, CMN-125), as caminito-git's optdepends names appmenu-gtk-module-caminito. Ubuntu's
# binary is appmenu-gtk3-module, and its epoch puts it above every stock version.
Recommends:
 appmenu-gtk3-module (>= 1:25.04-0caminito1),
 caminito-vscode,
 power-profiles-daemon,
 nm-connection-editor,
Suggests:
 libheif-examples,
Description: Wayland compositor for the MATE desktop
 Caminito is a Wayland compositor for MATE, the counterpart of Marco: it
 reads Marco's settings, draws its themes and binds its keys, so that MATE
 runs on Wayland as it does on X11.
 .
 This package has the compositor, caminito-displays, caminito-about, the
 wallpaper's drawer and Wallpaper dialog, Workspace Behaviour
 (caminito-behaviour), the palette and locker helpers,
 caminito-bluetooth, caminito-network, the Bluetooth, Power, Thermal and
 Network panel applets, and the "MATE on Caminito" session that display
 managers list.
